SRINAGAR: Nepal is grappling with its worst communal unrest in recent years after clashes between Hindu and Muslim communities in the country’s southern plains left three people dead, prompting curfews across multiple districts and appeals for peace from the country’s top leadership.

Follow Us On G -N e w s | Whatsapp

Prime Minister Balendra Shah on Thursday made his first major national address since assuming office in March, urging citizens to exercise restraint and help restore “peace, harmony, brotherhood and national unity” as violence spread from Sunsari district to neighbouring areas. He assured the nation that the government would conduct a “completely fair and transparent” investigation and bring those responsible to justice.

