The violence began on July 26 in Sunsari district, near the Indian border, following a dispute between members of the Hindu and Muslim communities over loud music and religious flags during a Hindu religious procession. According to police, attempts to disperse the crowd escalated into firing, leaving two people dead. A third person was killed on Thursday during protests in neighbouring Siraha district despite a curfew being in force.

