Authorities have imposed curfews in Sunsari and adjoining districts, while security forces remain on high alert to prevent further escalation. Police spokesperson Abi Narayan Kafle said personnel have been instructed to protect public property and restore normalcy while using minimal force.

The unrest has triggered political concern across Nepal. The Nepali Communist Party (NCP) has demanded an independent high-level judicial commission to investigate the killings, arguing that police action alone cannot resolve the deeper communal tensions in the Terai-Madhesh region. The party also urged its cadres to organise harmony rallies and work with local communities to prevent further violence.

